WEBVTT

1
00:00:11.667 --> 00:00:22.021
I wasn't sure how long I'd been at Birtwick Park, for horses don't keep track of time the way humans do.

2
00:00:22.022 --> 00:00:27.154
But it had been long enough for everything about the place to feel familiar.

3
00:00:27.155 --> 00:00:30.849
I was used to my life there, and to the horses and people.

4
00:00:30.850 --> 00:00:35.996
I never expected anything to change.

5
00:00:35.997 --> 00:00:38.952
Then one day the squire came to the stable.

6
00:00:38.953 --> 00:00:42.558
John Manly had just ridden me out for some exercise.

7
00:00:42.559 --> 00:00:48.830
Now he was grooming me while James fetched some oats from the shed where the horses' feed was stored.

8
00:00:48.831 --> 00:00:55.556
When the squire came over, his face was serious. He was holding a letter.

9
00:00:55.557 --> 00:01:00.174
John immediately noticed the squire's serious face.

10
00:01:00.175 --> 00:01:03.924
He quickly led me into my stall and shut the door behind me.

11
00:01:03.925 --> 00:01:06.669
Then he turned to face the squire.

12
00:01:06.670 --> 00:01:10.654
"Good morning, sir," he said. "What can I do for you?"

13
00:01:10.655 --> 00:01:16.061
"Good morning, John." The squire's voice was as serious as his face.

14
00:01:16.062 --> 00:01:21.592
"I need to ask you something. Do you have any complaints about young James?"

15
00:01:21.593 --> 00:01:25.316
James himself had just emerged from the feed shed.

16
00:01:25.317 --> 00:01:29.045
He stood there in the doorway looking surprised.

17
00:01:29.046 --> 00:01:36.247
But John was quick to answer. "Complaints, sir?" he said. "Absolutely not."

18
00:01:36.248 --> 00:01:39.372
"Is he a hard worker?" the squire asked.

19
00:01:39.373 --> 00:01:42.510
"Or does he get lazy when your back is turned?"

20
00:01:42.511 --> 00:01:45.385
"He works as hard as I do," John said.

21
00:01:45.386 --> 00:01:49.014
"I've never known him to be lazy about anything."

22
00:01:49.015 --> 00:01:53.794
"That's good." The squire glanced at the letter he was holding.

23
00:01:53.795 --> 00:01:56.766
"But now I have another question for you.

24
00:01:56.767 --> 00:02:03.852
When he goes out with the horses to exercise them or to deliver a message, does he do only what he's supposed to be doing?

25
00:02:03.853 --> 00:02:08.029
Or do you think he might sometimes stop to talk with his friends?"

26
00:02:08.030 --> 00:02:12.240
"I have no reason to suspect that," John said, frowning.

27
00:02:12.241 --> 00:02:18.676
"And if anybody has been saying that sort of thing about James, I want to know who it is.

28
00:02:18.677 --> 00:02:23.799
James is the most honest young man I know, and the hardest worker too.

29
00:02:23.800 --> 00:02:30.082
He's gentle and clever with the horses, and I never worry about leaving him in charge when I have to go somewhere.

30
00:02:30.083 --> 00:02:33.293
If anyone wants to say otherwise, send him to me!"

31
00:02:33.294 --> 00:02:39.735
The squire's serious look disappeared. He chuckled and glanced over at James.

32
00:02:39.736 --> 00:02:43.202
"Come on out, young man," he said to him.

33
00:02:43.203 --> 00:02:47.345
"I'm glad to hear that John's opinion of you is the same as my own.

34
00:02:47.346 --> 00:02:51.189
Now let me tell you why I needed to hear it."

35
00:02:51.190 --> 00:02:55.721
James came out to the yard. He looked nervous.

36
00:02:55.722 --> 00:03:02.624
"What is it, sir?" he asked. "Has someone been saying bad things about me?"

37
00:03:02.625 --> 00:03:08.188
"Not at all, my boy," the squire assured him. "I'm sorry to worry you.

38
00:03:08.189 --> 00:03:12.100
But I needed to make sure I got John's honest opinion.

39
00:03:12.101 --> 00:03:15.220
You see, my brother-in-law just wrote to me."

40
00:03:15.221 --> 00:03:17.452
He held up the letter.

41
00:03:17.453 --> 00:03:21.201
Then he explained that his brother-in-law was looking for a groom.

42
00:03:21.202 --> 00:03:25.354
"His old coachman has been with him for thirty years," he went on.

43
00:03:25.355 --> 00:03:30.160
"He wants a young man to work with him for a few years and take over when he retires.

44
00:03:30.161 --> 00:03:35.174
It would be a good job, with a fair salary and a nice place to live."

45
00:03:35.175 --> 00:03:39.014
"Oh," John said slowly. "I see.

46
00:03:39.015 --> 00:03:42.810
Well, I'll miss James if he takes the job, sir.

47
00:03:42.811 --> 00:03:46.501
But nobody deserves a good opportunity more than he does."

48
00:03:46.502 --> 00:03:53.459
"I agree," the squire said. "So do you think he can do the job?"

49
00:03:53.460 --> 00:03:59.650
"Yes, I do," John replied. "He doesn't have much experience in driving yet.

50
00:03:59.651 --> 00:04:04.340
But he can do everything else there is to do around the stable, and do it well.

51
00:04:04.341 --> 00:04:08.600
Your brother-in-law would be lucky to have him."

52
00:04:08.601 --> 00:04:12.063
I was listening along with the other horses.

53
00:04:12.064 --> 00:04:16.979
At first I didn't understand all of what the men were saying.

54
00:04:16.980 --> 00:04:21.605
But Merrylegs, who understands humans better than any of us, figured it out.

55
00:04:21.606 --> 00:04:26.342
James was going to be leaving us in about a month to work at another stable.

56
00:04:26.343 --> 00:04:34.818
In the meantime he needed practice driving the carriage as much as he could.

57
00:04:34.819 --> 00:04:39.896
For the next few weeks, the carriage went out more than ever before.

58
00:04:39.897 --> 00:04:44.590
Normally the squire only used it when his wife was going somewhere with him.

59
00:04:44.591 --> 00:04:49.774
But now Ginger and I were hitched to the carriage for every errand, no matter how small.

60
00:04:49.775 --> 00:04:55.758
At first John rode along to give instructions while James drove.

61
00:04:55.759 --> 00:04:59.568
After a while James was allowed to take us out by himself.

62
00:04:59.569 --> 00:05:03.679
His driving got better all the time.

63
00:05:03.680 --> 00:05:07.582
Finally the squire decided it was time for the final test.

64
00:05:07.583 --> 00:05:12.822
He and his wife wanted to pay a visit to some friends who lived about fifty miles away.

65
00:05:12.823 --> 00:05:19.949
It would be a two-day trip, and James would drive them there and back.
